{"type":"standard","title":"Wunambal language","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Wunambal language</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q3913805","titles":{"canonical":"Wunambal_language","normalized":"Wunambal language","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Wunambal language</span></span>"},"pageid":5455174,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Worrorran_map.svg/330px-Worrorran_map.svg.png","width":330,"height":344},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Worrorran_map.svg/960px-Worrorran_map.svg.png","width":786,"height":820},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1339103625","tid":"d42d0e88-0d21-11f1-8870-fc60d1f30f5a","timestamp":"2026-02-18T23:30:37Z","description":"Aboriginal Australian language of Western Australia","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wunambal_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wunambal_language?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wunambal_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Wunambal_language"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wunambal_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Wunambal_language","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wunambal_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Wunambal_language"}},"extract":"The Wunambal language, also known as Northern Worrorran, Gamberre, or Gambera, is a moribund Australian Aboriginal language of Western Australia. It has several dialects, including Yiiji, Gunin, Miwa, and Wilawila. It is spoken by the Wunambal people.","extract_html":"<p>The <b>Wunambal language</b>, also known as <b>Northern Worrorran</b>, <b>Gamberre</b>, or <b>Gambera</b>, is a moribund Australian Aboriginal language of Western Australia. It has several dialects, including <b>Yiiji</b>, <b>Gunin</b>, <b>Miwa</b>, and <b>Wilawila</b>. It is spoken by the Wunambal people.</p>"}